   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Pulsing Border\n\nA glowing, pulsing frame of light runs around the edges of the frame and leaves the center clear for content, drawn in WebGL.\n\nCategory: shaders. Length: 5 s. WebGL: yes.\n\nUse when:\n- You want a pulsing lit frame around the scene edges to contain foreground content.\n- A premium reveal benefits from an edge glow that leaves the center clear for text.\n- You want corner radius and thickness tunable via `roundness` and `thickness`.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The brief bans decorative glow: keep `bloom` and `intensity` restrained so the border does not read as neon.\n- You want a full-field texture: the interior stays mostly the background color; use a noise or gradient shader.\n- The scene already has a strong border or frame in the layout.\n\nVariables:\n- speed (number, 0-4): Speed, default 1\n- colors (string): Colors, default \"#52527a, #8a8a95, #3a3a5c\"\n- color_back (color): Background, default \"#12121a\"\n- roundness (number, 0-1): Roundness, default 0.25\n- thickness (number, 0-1): Thickness, default 0.1\n- softness (number, 0-1): Softness, default 0.75\n- intensity (number, 0-1): Intensity, default 0.2\n- bloom (number, 0-1): Bloom, default 0.25\n- spots (number, 1-5): Spots, default 4\n- spot_size (number, 0-1): Spot size, default 0.5\n- pulse (number, 0-1): Pulse, default 0.25\n- smoke (number, 0-1): Smoke, default 0.3\n- smoke_size (number, 0-1): Smoke size, default 0.6\n- margin (number, 0-0.5): Margin, default 0\n- rotation (number, 0-360): Rotation, default 0\n- scale (number, 0.1-4): Scale, default 1\n- resolution (number, 0.25-1): Resolution, default 0.75\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
